From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:24:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] vbscript: assigning to the name of a host named item declares
 a script variable (3020)

Set wsh = CreateObject("WScript.Shell") failed under cscript because WSH is a
named item of the script host, and an assignment that resolves to a named item
returned E_NOTIMPL. Such a name now behaves like any undeclared name: the
assignment declares a script-level variable (an error under Option Explicit),
and later uses of the name find that variable first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS

diff --git a/dlls/vbscript/interp.c b/dlls/vbscript/interp.c
index 2af9636..2467002 100644
--- a/dlls/vbscript/interp.c
+++ b/dlls/vbscript/interp.c
@@ -912,12 +912,12 @@ static HRESULT assign_ident(exec_ctx_t *ctx, BSTR name, WORD flags, DISPPARAMS *
     case REF_FUNC:
         FIXME("functions not implemented\n");
         return E_NOTIMPL;
-    case REF_OBJ:
-        FIXME("REF_OBJ\n");
-        return E_NOTIMPL;
     case REF_CONST:
         FIXME("REF_CONST\n");
         return E_NOTIMPL;
+    case REF_OBJ:
+        /* A host named item (like WScript or WSH) is not a variable: assigning to its name declares a
+         * script variable of that name, which then hides the item. */
     case REF_NONE:
         if(ctx->func->code_ctx->option_explicit) {
             /* Stained Glass OS 1652: the error Windows raises */
diff --git a/dlls/vbscript/tests/run.c b/dlls/vbscript/tests/run.c
index 8aaafbe..91ab207 100644
--- a/dlls/vbscript/tests/run.c
+++ b/dlls/vbscript/tests/run.c
@@ -3236,6 +3236,9 @@ static void run_tests(void)
     parse_script_w(L"Option Explicit\nset test.setobj = testObj");
     CHECK_CALLED(global_setobj_i);
 
+    /* assigning to the name of a host named item declares a script variable that hides the item */
+    parse_script_w(L"test = 3\ncall ok(test = 3, \"test = \" & test)\nset test = testObj\ncall ok(isObject(test), \"test is not an object\")");
+
     hres = parse_script_wr(L"dim x\nx = testObj.rem");
     ok(hres == S_OK, "use of 'rem' as dot identifier failed: %lx08\n", hres);
 
